      "summary": ": Friday 31 July 2026 POWDER DAY. ❄️ Wake up and smell the powder — Treble Cone has been absolutely hammered with fresh snow overnight, with 40cm of new snow on the upper mountain in the past 24 hours. It's light and dry up top, with a slightly heavier, denser snowpack down at the base — but make no mistake, this is exactly the kind of morning you set the alarm early for. And it's not stopping. The forecast has snow continuing through the day, with the snow line possibly dropping as low as 400m. That means road conditions will be affected — please drive with care and carry chains, no exceptions today. Lift Status: Home Basin — aiming to open by 9am Saddle Basin — Unfortunately The Saddle Basin will remain CLOSED today. Winds - We are forecast to see strong winds building during the day which may interrupt operations on the Saddle Quad Grooming: With snowy overnight conditions we'll only have Triple Treat, Main Street and the Beginner Platter groomed today ~ powder turns everywhere else! Rug up, bring your powder skis, and get ready for a proper day on the mountain. See you out there!",
      "webcam": {
        "page_url": "https://www.mountainwatch.com/new-zealand/treble-cone/snow-cams",
        "image_url": "https://www.mountainwatch.com/Resort/Treble-Cone-Home-Basin/LiveStill.jpg",
